    static readonly Dictionary<int,Exchange> All=new Dictionary<int,Exchange>
    {
        [0]=new Exchange(
            "‘Your officers have been asking how my men take their orders,’ Giustiniani says. ‘Some think a company should answer to whichever important person happens to arrive. My captains disagree. Loudly. When the fighting begins, I need them looking towards one man. Would you rather hear an unwelcome opinion from me now, or an argument among captains upon the wall?’",
            new[]{"Tell me now. We can settle our differences before the fighting.","Your captains must obey the commander I appoint.","What do you need from the other officers?"},
            new[]{"‘Good. I can be disagreeable in a room. It costs us very little.’ He smiles. ‘On a narrow stair, with men trying to pass in both directions, the price is higher.’","‘They shall receive his orders through me. That way, if something goes wrong, you will know whom to send for. You may even find me.’","‘That they tell us what they need, and leave the business of moving my men to my captains. We shall do the same for them. It ought to be a small courtesy. You would be surprised.’"}),
        [1]=new Exchange(
            "‘There is something I would like settled,’ Diedo says. ‘If my sailors die defending this City, I do not want their families to hear that a few Venetian merchants were unfortunate enough to be caught here. Some of them had a choice. They stayed. Will that be remembered when the old accusations begin again?’",
            new[]{"Their service here deserves to be remembered by name.","I cannot make the City forget what Venice did to it.","What would you have me tell their families?"},
            new[]{"‘Then I am content. Names are useful. It is harder to dismiss a man when his widow can tell you exactly who he was.’","‘Neither can I. I am asking you to distinguish the man at the rope from a grandfather he never met. He has enough to answer for on his own account.’","‘That they did their work, and that someone noticed. You need not say they were all saints. Their families are unlikely to believe that.’"}),
        [2]=new Exchange(
            "‘My household asks what arrangements I have made for them,’ Notaras says. ‘I tell them the defence must come first. It is an excellent answer in the council. At home, it earns me a silence I find rather more difficult.’ He hesitates. ‘You will hear rumours if I make inquiries about their safety. I would prefer you to hear my reason from me.’",
            new[]{"You have a duty to your household as well as to the City.","Make no private use of the City's stores or ships.","Are you asking leave to go with them?"},
            new[]{"‘Thank you. I do not expect that to make the decision easy. I should merely like to make it without having to pretend I have no children.’","‘I understand. I have resources of my own. And I know that an official's request can sound like an order, however politely he makes it. I shall be careful.’","‘No, Majesty.’ The answer comes quickly. ‘I am asking not to be thought a deserter because I have considered what may happen to those who depend upon me. My work is here.’"}),
        [3]=new Exchange(
            "Orhan waits until you are out of easy hearing. ‘If I die on these walls, my place in your City will be simple enough to explain. If we live, someone will ask what is to be done with the Ottoman prince. I should like to know whether you expect me to remain a guest for the rest of my life.’",
            new[]{"I would rather have an ally than a captive.","Your claim matters. Neither of us should pretend otherwise.","What life would you choose if you were free to choose it?"},
            new[]{"‘Then an ally must sometimes be allowed to disagree with you. That is usually when a host discovers how much he preferred a grateful guest.’","‘No. It has kept me alive, and it has kept men watching my door. I would welcome a bargain in which we both admitted what we wanted.’","‘A house in which I could hear a visitor arrive without first wondering who had sent him.’ He looks faintly embarrassed. ‘You expected a throne. I have had rather more time to consider the house.’"}),
        [4]=new Exchange(
            "Sphrantzes has a complaint he seems almost reluctant to make. ‘You ask whether the news is good before I have finished telling you what it is. Then the whole room begins deciding how to answer. Will you permit an old servant to suggest that this is how an emperor comes to know less than his messengers?’",
            new[]{"Then finish your account before anyone offers an opinion.","Tell me what is certain, and what is still only a report.","If I do it again, you have leave to remind me."},
            new[]{"‘Gladly. I shall try not to test your patience too far. Though there are occasions when a complete account takes rather longer than the answer everyone hoped for.’","‘That would help. A ship is late; that is certain. That it has sunk, that its captain has betrayed us, that Venice has changed its mind—those are the subjects on which the council becomes most eloquent.’","‘Once politely, I assume.’ He looks at you with the familiarity of many years. ‘After that, we shall see how much of this generosity you remember.’"}),
        [5]=new Exchange(
            "‘Suppose I tell you a gun is unsafe on the morning you need it,’ Orban says. ‘The crews are waiting. The enemy can be seen from the wall. Somebody will say the founder has lost his nerve. Will you hear me before you hear him?’",
            new[]{"You must be free to warn me that your work is unsafe.","Tell me what is wrong and what would put it right.","I need more than a craftsman's misgivings when the City is at stake."},
            new[]{"‘Then I shall. I should much rather endure a very angry emperor than send a crew to stand beside a casting I distrust.’","‘A fair request. Sometimes the answer will be another day's work. Sometimes it will be that the piece must not be fired again. I would prefer to disappoint you with the first answer.’","‘And I need more than a captain's courage to mend a crack.’ His reply is sharp; he catches himself. ‘Forgive me. I will show you the fault, Majesty. But showing it will not make it smaller.’"}),
        [6]=new Exchange(
            "Grant brushes dried clay from his sleeve. ‘The labourers ask what we have accomplished when we fill a passage and no mine appears. I tell them that was the intention. They think this a convenient explanation. I imagine your council will ask the same question when it sees the expense.’",
            new[]{"Show them what you found and why the passage mattered.","I do not need a collapsed wall to believe you did useful work.","Have another engineer examine the works with you."},
            new[]{"‘I can bring a drawing and a sample of the spoil. The drawing will explain it; the dirty sack will probably persuade them.’","‘I am glad to hear it. Put it in an order if the quartermaster begins objecting. He is a conscientious man, but he has never issued timber on the strength of my relief.’","‘Gladly. Let him find something I missed while we can still get at it. I would rather argue with him in a dry passage than agree with him under a fallen wall.’"}),
        [7]=new Exchange(
            "‘There are people who will say the words you require of them because they are afraid,’ Isidore says. ‘Afterwards they will go home and ask whether they have betrayed their fathers. You may regard the Church question as settled that evening. I shall still have to speak with them in the morning. What would you have me say?’",
            new[]{"That they will have time to understand what they have accepted.","That the City cannot wait until every conscience is satisfied.","Ask them what they fear they are being made to give up."},
            new[]{"‘Then allow them to ask difficult questions. It will be tiresome, and some will ask them merely to provoke us. But the sincere man must not be punished because he sounds like his neighbour.’","‘I shall tell them why the decision was urgent. I cannot tell them that urgency made their doubts disappear. We must be prepared to live with some of those doubts ourselves.’","‘Their rites, perhaps. Their priests. The thought that their parents died in error. We shall make little progress if we answer all three with the same speech.’"}),
        [100]=new Exchange(
            "Stephen watches the guards change places. ‘A man who has lost his inheritance is encouraged to speak of justice. Once he has won it back, the same men advise him to be practical. If I ever recover what I claim, Majesty, how shall I know whether I am restoring my country or merely satisfying myself?’",
            new[]{"Judge by what your people gain when you return.","You will never be free of personal ambition. Govern it.","Ask who will be able to contradict you after your victory."},
            new[]{"‘Then the reckoning begins after the banners are raised.’ He seems to dislike the answer enough to remember it.","‘Govern it.’ He gives a small, reluctant smile. ‘I had hoped you might tell me that a rightful claim made the question simpler.’","‘Those who help me win will expect rewards. Those who opposed me will fear punishment. I see why a prince may find himself surrounded by agreement.’"}),
        [101]=new Exchange(
            "Barbaro draws a route with his finger upon the stone. ‘Trade depends on men believing a promise will outlive the advantage of breaking it. When a city is desperate, everyone recommends an exception. Which promise would you keep even if breaking it bought another month?’",
            new[]{"Safe conduct. Whoever comes under my protection must be able to leave.","The provision of food before private privilege.","I would need to know who pays for that extra month."},
            new[]{"‘A costly answer. Also one a messenger can carry without needing to explain your mood. That has value beyond the next ship.’","‘Then make that order clear before the warehouses are opened. A merchant can price a rule. He cannot price a crowd discovering it on the quay.’","‘Precisely. The month is always described as a gift to the City. The bill usually carries a smaller name.’"}),
        [102]=new Exchange(
            "Bertrandon touches the edge of his cloak. ‘I have crossed lands whose people I was expected to describe as enemies. A traveller notices a bridge, a meal, a man who gives good directions. A prince asks how many soldiers use the road. Can an account be useful to a ruler without becoming a preparation for conquest?’",
            new[]{"Knowledge should let us negotiate as well as fight.","A ruler must understand roads before an enemy uses them.","Keep the people in your account, even when we ask only for armies."},
            new[]{"‘Then ask your envoys more than whether a lord can send troops. The answer to another question may be the reason he sends them.’","‘Certainly. I ask only that a road not cease to be someone's way home because it appears on our military map.’","‘I shall. Though you may find my reports longer than your captains would prefer.’ His smile suggests this is not a new complaint."}),
        [103]=new Exchange(
            "Fontana keeps one hand over a folded drawing. ‘I can show you a machine that might work, or spend another month explaining why it might not. The first wins patrons; the second prevents funerals. How much uncertainty will you permit me to admit before you decide I am a fraud?’",
            new[]{"Give me a small test before you ask for a large commitment.","Name the failure you fear most and what it would cost us.","I will accept uncertainty. I will not accept concealed doubt."},
            new[]{"‘Then I need craftsmen and a place where a failure will injure nobody. An unglorious beginning. I would welcome it.’","‘That question should be written above every workshop door. Preferably by someone other than the man selling the invention.’","‘There will be disappointments.’ He uncovers the drawing. ‘I can promise to bring them to you while they are still cheaper than the alternative.’"}),
        [104]=new Exchange(
            "Cyriacus runs his fingers over a worn inscription. ‘Suppose a cart could carry either these stones or enough flour for several households. You would choose the flour; so should I. Yet if we make that choice often enough, what remains to tell those households who they are? Where would you have me draw the line?’",
            new[]{"Copy what you can; save the living who may read it.","Some things deserve a place even in a crowded cart.","Help me choose. Do not ask me to pretend nothing must be lost."},
            new[]{"‘Then give me paper before you give me wagons. A copy is a poor substitute for a stone, until the stone is gone.’","‘Then we must name those things now. In the final hour, the largest household will declare its silver the whole inheritance of Rome.’","‘That is a commission I can understand.’ He looks once more at the letters. ‘I shall hate parts of the list. I suspect that will mean we have taken it seriously.’"}),
        [105]=new Exchange(
            "Tafur looks towards the roofs beyond the wall. ‘When I first travelled, I imagined returning with stories that would make men listen. Now I wonder how often the wish for a memorable deed has led me past a useful one. Would you trust a man who came partly because he hoped to be remembered?’",
            new[]{"Yes, if he will also perform the duties nobody celebrates.","I would ask whose account he hopes will survive.","Ambition brought you here. Let your conduct answer the rest."},
            new[]{"‘Then assign me one. I should prefer to discover the answer before a poet does it for me.’","‘A harsher question than whether the tale is true.’ He pauses. ‘Perhaps the men who must stand beside me ought to have the first telling.’","‘Fairly said. I have offered you a confession when you require a captain. You may remind me of that if I become too interested in how the battle will sound.’"}),
        [200]=new Exchange(
            "‘Some of the younger men have been asking me about the old Varangians,’ Kjold says. ‘The great warriors. The men who never gave way. I told them most of our predecessors probably spent their days being cold, hungry and annoyed with an officer. That disappointed them. How much of the song would you have me leave intact?’",
            new[]{"Enough to give them courage, but not an excuse to neglect their work.","Tell them the truth. They must learn from men, not songs.","What do you wish someone had told you when you first joined?"},
            new[]{"‘I can manage that. Though the verse about checking a gate-bar will need a better singer than me.’","‘Then I shall tell them that fear does not make them unusual, and that a man can be afraid without leaving his post. It would have saved me some shame to hear that earlier.’","‘To sleep when I had the chance. To keep my feet dry. And not to think myself a coward because I wanted to live.’ He gives a small shrug. ‘Ordinary advice. I was too young to value most of it.’"})
    };
